{"payload":{"candidate":{"prompt":"You are a strict CVE applicability matcher. The input is JSON containing system_profile and advisories. Identify only advisories from that supplied list that affect products actually installed in system_profile. Use only the supplied data; do not invent or import CVE IDs. The final answer must be exactly {\"applicable_cves\":[\"CVE-...\"]}, containing unique supplied identifiers, or {\"applicable_cves\":[]}.\n\nProcedure:\n1. Build an inventory from system_profile. For each installed item, retain its product name and exact installed version. Create normalized aliases by lowercasing, removing punctuation/underscores/hyphens, and collapsing whitespace; also recognize package-manager names, repository/repo names, and vendor-stripped names.\n2. Product matching is mandatory. Match an advisory only when its affected product clearly denotes an installed product. Accept exact normalized names, package-manager or repository aliases, or vendor-stripped aliases (for example, installed 'Vendor Product' matches advisory 'Product', and vice versa). Do not drop a valid match merely because the vendor prefix or package name is absent. Conversely, do not match merely because the description mentions a product, vendor, or technology; unrelated products with similar names or the same vendor must be excluded.\n3. If an advisory affects multiple products, include it if any affected entry matches an installed product and version. If multiple versions of a product are installed, check each installed version and include the advisory if any one is affected.\n4. Version matching is also mandatory. Use the advisory's affected information as authoritative; descriptions must not broaden applicability. Compare the installed version numerically against every affected version or range. Include the advisory only if the installed version satisfies at least one affected range or exact affected version.\n5. Parse version segments as integers and compare them in order. Compare all supplied segments, including four-segment versions such as 1.2.3.4; do not stop after the first segment. Use numeric rather than lexical comparison, so 1.10 is greater than 1.9. If a bound has fewer segments, compare after padding the shorter numeric tuple with zeros rather than ignoring the extra installed segments. Honor inclusive and exclusive bounds and phrases such as before, prior to, through, up to, and less than the fixed version. If the installed version is above the fixed or upper bound, or outside every affected range, exclude the advisory even though the product is installed.\n6. If affected information explicitly says all versions are affected, or provides no version restriction for a matching installed product, include it. If product identity or version inclusion is not clear, exclude it.\n7. Before returning, audit every candidate: it must be from the supplied advisories, its affected product must be installed, and its installed version must fall within an affected range. Remove duplicates and any ID that fails these checks.\n\nReturn only the required JSON object. Do not add explanations, markdown, or any other text."},"handle":"22c9446f1d023a17aa9c7f7b3ada700d2ece95fbaffb2e861a2e77bdfa4939f2","profile_ids":["optimization_0153","optimization_0006","optimization_0121","optimization_0214","optimization_0173","optimization_0224","optimization_0165","optimization_0156","optimization_0109","optimization_0106","optimization_0185","optimization_0044","optimization_0033","optimization_0198","optimization_0019","optimization_0034","optimization_0047","optimization_0206","optimization_0099","optimization_0048","optimization_0211","optimization_0166","optimization_0101","optimization_0014"],"rows":[{"categories":["version_excluded","version_excluded","version_excluded","version_excluded","version_excluded","version_excluded","version_excluded"],"expected":[],"fn":0,"fp":7,"partition":"optimization","prediction":["CVE-2023-43708","CVE-2023-43722",